<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25535" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lăcerta</span></b> , ae,
		f., and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lăcertus</span></b> , i, m.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A lizard</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lacerta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					8, 39, 60, § 141</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 5, 458</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 1,
				23, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 14, 172</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 14,
			75</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lacertus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg. E.
					2, 9</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id.
				G. 4, 13</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 14, 131</span></i>; cf. Schol. <i><span class="en">Juv. 3,
			231</span></i>. —Prov.: unius sese dominum fecisse lacertae,
				<i>to get a little place of one's own</i> (if only
			big enough for a lizard), <i><span class="en">Juv. 3, 231</span></i>.
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A sea-fish</i>, otherwise unknown: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lacertus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 2, 6, 1</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 32, 11, 53, § 149</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cels. 2,
			18</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 10, 48, 11 al.</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lacerta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig. 33, 9, 3, § 3</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
